           /*benefit=*/2);
+      // FMA fallback (e.g. f32): rebalance the blocked per-thread tile to cut
+      // LDS read volume. Lower benefit than WMMA so it only fires when the dot
+      // stays blocked (i.e. not mapped to WMMA).
